%description:

Tcp.maxRexmitCount:zero -- the connection aborts at the first timeout, without a retransmission.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the retransmissions of one segment, after which the connection aborts";
with 0, there is no retransmission.

The classes: limit (1 and more; 12 is the default, 15 the value of LinuxTcp) and zero (0).
The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::processRexmitTimer() aborts the connection when the count of
retransmissions of a segment exceeds the value. This test separates "zero" from "limit".

Host under test: host1, with 0 and without the tail loss probe, which sends 100 bytes; the tap
drops each data segment. Observation: level 1, one data segment of host1, and the abort at
the application 1 s later.

%# parameter: Tcp.maxRexmitCount
%# class: zero
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.maxRexmitCount
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMaxRexmitCountZero")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").drop()
                     .describe("each data segment of host1"))
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
            app.sendData(app.socket(), 100);
        }))
        .meanwhile(exactlyTimes(1, on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                       .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                                       .describe("a data segment of host1")
                                       .within(3.0)))
        .once(on("host1.app[0]").signal("socketFailure")
                  .notBefore(0.9)
                  .describe("the abort of the connection")
                  .within(1.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMaxRexmitCountZero compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.maxRexmitCount = 0    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMaxRexmitCountZero: PASS
